  "status_text": "A pattern we had only seen by computer is now checked for every size: a cycle running through n rows and n columns never needs more than 3n - 1 gates. For every n from 3, the 2n-cycle (row i joined to columns i and i + 1 mod n) is represented with at most 3n - 1 AND/OR gates of fan-in at most two [L-meta-19185], and a checked floor puts it at no less than 2n - 1 + ceil((n - 1)/4) [L-meta-17154]; the true cost sits between the two.",
